; Test: Negative conclusion propagation
; Coverage: -d cascades through rule chains, discarding downstream rules

; Chain: a => b => c
; But b is contested by ~b with no superiority, so b is ambiguous.
; Since -d b, the rule b => c is discarded, so -d c too.
(given a)
(given x)
(normally r1 a b)
(normally r2 x (not b))
(normally r3 b c)

; b is ambiguous (r1 vs r2, no superiority) => -d b, -d ~b
; c depends on b, so r3 is discarded => -d c
; EXPECT: +D a
; EXPECT: +d a
; EXPECT: +D x
; EXPECT: +d x
; EXPECT: -d b
; EXPECT: -d ~b
; EXPECT: -d c
